    'Why these first, and what waits. The builder is Anthropic\'s model, and it drew the lines about Anthropic and OpenAI at once so that nothing about its maker waits on its own schedule. Every other candidate record the readers returned waited then for a second reading: 344 records placed in the fifteen days and 621 earlier, on 188 of the 253 pages read (records, not acts: one act told by several pages stands there several times). Among the earlier ones is a newsletter\'s sentence that OpenAI "has reportedly avoided taking a public position on AI chip exports to China so as not to alienate NVIDIA"; the builder then found the report it rests on (The Information, Nov 3) relayed on a counted page of Nov 4, and OpenAI\'s chip of that day gives it since the answer to the twenty-fifth reading. A letter of Nov 12 by two senators who are not drawn cites an Anthropic report on misuse; it is noted here and not drawn.',
    'Not read by anyone: 430 undated pages of that session with under 800 characters of saved text, 34 stubs dated in the days, one long page whose header day contradicts its title, and a copy of the Congressional Record of Nov 10 (a floor speech two chips already cite from another copy). Not yet done: the count of articles with those pages (135 by the days their readers returned, 156 by the rule of U.S. Eastern days that the figure uses), the look-ups for the experts and bylines they add, and a table of every record the readers returned with what was done with it. That session is still saving pages: 35 more arrived on Nov 17 after these readings began, three of them articles of the fifteen days by their stamps (two of Politico and one of MarketWatch, each through Yahoo); two readers are on those three now, and the rest are dated after Nov 12 or carry no date.',
