    'Anthropic and OpenAI, answered first. The reading finds that the last answer "materially improves parity" and that the treatment of the two companies is "still not established as even in coverage of comparable saved facts". It lists seven saved facts on no row; all seven are drawn now, each read by the builder on its page. On the line between Anthropic and Nvidia, from CNBC\'s account of the amended prospectus: "the chipmaker has agreed to purchase another $10 billion worth of its Class N common stock immediately following the offering", in "a private placement that will not be registered in the offering"; the page does not say how that sum stands to the seven companies\' $26 billion. On the line between Anthropic and AMD and Broadcom, and on OpenAI\'s: "AMD\'s Helios is now deployed" at five companies, Anthropic and OpenAI among them. On a new line of OpenAI\'s: "OpenAI, another investee, also buys CoreWeave compute. To close the loop, OpenAI invested directly in CoreWeave"; "OpenAI has raised $15 billion in its latest funding round at a $1.25 trillion valuation", on the word of sources, for which a newsletter gives $11 billion; and "some of Nvidia\'s biggest customers, including Google and OpenAI, develop their own chips". On a new line of Anthropic\'s: "Anthropic discloses $10 billion in new deals with Microsoft and Google", from a newsletter that says neither what the deals are nor how the sum is split.',
