    'One rule for summaries with no occasion. Three of the five readers of the earlier passages had set aside summaries in which they found no identifiable occasion (a position a company "has said", lobbying over months); two had kept comparable ones as unresolved. The reading named one pair; by the readers\' own wording about a third of the kept groups are undated or unidentified as well. One rule holds now for every actor: such a summary is registered as an open, unresolved record and marked so. 43 groups (48 lines) joined the register by it; 10 lines stay set aside, of groups a reader found not to be the actor\'s or not on the matter. Since no reader had compared the 43 with the chips, the builder did: five are carried by a chip that quotes or gives the same sentence, one is carried in part, 37 are on no chip. The register\'s open count is therefore not a count of identified occasions. No reader has read this change.',
