    'Because the first screen had missed that chip, a second looked at every chip dated by a report (175): 34 cite a page that links some post, and for five the link is to an account whose handle holds the actor\'s surname. Two are posts quoted a day late and moved: Alec Stapp\'s of Nov 9, which a newsletter quotes on Nov 10 ("Expect it to keep getting worse"), and an investor\'s of Nov 8, which a blog quotes on Nov 9. One is a statement to a news agency and not a post; one\'s posts are of the chip\'s own day. The fifth is Anthropic\'s chip on the filing it sent and retracted: the listing page links two posts of Anthropic\'s own account, and the builder fetched and read both. One announces two models and is not on the matter. The other is of Nov 10: "Anthropic has launched the roadshow for its proposed initial public offering". Neither says anything of the retracted filing, so that chip stands as it was; Anthropic\'s chip of Nov 10, which had said that no page gave the launch a day, now cites the company\'s own post for it.',
